            <section ID="LINK_7a1fe5c3-7a8b-4fe0-a6fc-63dab8f7c32c">
               <id root="22f51c4b-ce2b-4eb7-aa77-6a4e5fc88f7b"/>
               <code code="34089-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="DESCRIPTION SECTION"/>
               <title>DESCRIPTION</title>
               <text>
                  <paragraph>Baclofen, USP is a muscle relaxant and antispastic.</paragraph>
                  <paragraph>Its chemical name is 4-amino-3-(4-chlorophenyl)-butanoic acid. The structural formula is:</paragraph>
                  <renderMultiMedia referencedObject="MM1"/>
                  <paragraph>Baclofen, USP is a white to creamy white powder. It is slightly soluble in water, very slightly soluble in methanol, and insoluble in chloroform.</paragraph>
                  <paragraph>Baclofen Tablets USP 10 mg and 20 mg contain the following inactive ingredients: colloidal silicon dioxide, crospovidone, magnesium stearate, microcrystalline cellulose and pregelatinized starch.<br/>
                  </paragraph>
               </text>
               <effectiveTime value="20241107"/>
               <component>
                  <observationMedia ID="MM1">
                     <text>This is an image of the structural formula for Baclofen.</text>
                     <value xsi:type="ED" mediaType="image/jpeg">
                        <reference value="baclofentabs-1.jpg"/>
                     </value>
                  </observationMedia>
               </component>
            </section>
         </component>
